<crash-analysis>
The crash is a stack-buffer-overflow in `AffixMgr::compound_check_morph`. The variable `st`, which is a `std::string`, has a length of 1. However, the code attempts to access `st[3]`, leading to an out-of-bounds read.

The root cause is a logic error in the `compound_check_morph` function. It does not properly validate the index `i` against the length of the string `st` before accessing it.

To fix this, a bounds check should be added before the access to `st[i]`. For example:

```c++
if (i < st.length()) {
ch = st[i];
} else {
// Handle the error, e.g., by breaking the loop or returning an error.
break; 
}
```
This will prevent the out-of-bounds read and make the code more robust against unexpected inputs.
</crash-analysis>

